File Transfer Commands
1️⃣ Copy file to remote server
scp file.txt user@remote_ip:/path/

2️⃣ Copy folder to remote server
scp -r folder/ user@remote_ip:/path/

3️⃣ Copy file from remote to local
scp user@remote_ip:/path/file.txt /local/path/

4️⃣ Copy between two remote servers
scp user1@server1:/path/file user2@server2:/path/

5️⃣ Use custom SSH port
scp -P 2222 file.txt user@ip:/path/

6️⃣ Copy using SSH key authentication
scp -i key.pem file.txt user@ip:/path/

🔹 Rsync Commands
1️⃣ Copy file (local → remote)
rsync file.txt user@remote_ip:/path/

2️⃣ Copy folder
rsync -avz folder/ user@remote_ip:/path/

3️⃣ Remote → Local
rsync -avz user@remote_ip:/path/folder/ /local/path/

4️⃣ Delete extra files in destination
rsync -avz --delete src/ user@remote_ip:/dest/

5️⃣ Rsync with SSH key and port
rsync -avz -e "ssh -i key.pem -p 22" folder/ user@ip:/path/
